============================================================
ARRAY SUMMATION LOGIC:
============================================================

1. 0-Based Indexing:
   - In C, array indices always run from 0 to n - 1[cite: 13].
   - Therefore, the loops run with condition 'i < n'[cite: 13].

2. Variable Length Array (VLA):
   - 'int num[n];' allocates the array dynamically on the stack 
     after 'n' is scanned at runtime (supported since C99)[cite: 13].

3. Accumulator Pattern:
   - Variable 's' must start at 0 so prior garbage memory does 
     not corrupt the summation[cite: 13].


