============================================================
SECOND LARGEST ELEMENT LOGIC:
============================================================

1. Single Pass Efficiency:
   - Finds the second largest element in O(n) linear time without 
     the overhead of sorting algorithms (which take O(n log n) or O(n^2)).

2. Role of INT_MIN (<limits.h>):
   - Initializing 'max' and 's_max' to INT_MIN ensures the algorithm 
     functions properly even if the user enters negative numbers[cite: 16].

3. Update Mechanism:
